fidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56827, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Vg82vL7oDD2Pdd6Un3Dqu3", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56827, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Vg82vL7oDD2Pdd6Un3Dqu3", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58564, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01SHF1tFmTi2zxtAx1ji5Zyg", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58864, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01SHF1tFmTi2zxtAx1ji5Zyg", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58864, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01SHF1tFmTi2zxtAx1ji5Zyg", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 64018, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001. The service is healthy again, with the error rate down from about 18% to 0.2%.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy. v2.3.1 and its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, were both unhealthy.\n  - The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left the regions on different versions: us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1.\n  - Repeating a rollback to a healthy version is safe, so I ran it again. This time it finished, and all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0.\n- **Incident:** My request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so I didn't retry. That avoided a second page to the on-call engineer.\n  - INC-0001 covers what went wrong, the rollback and the partial failure, and the current state.\n  - It lists two follow-ups: find the cause of the v2.3.1 problem (including why the release went out when its candidate was already unhealthy), and investigate the orchestrator error.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GcC3P7RLMeGf6iJyWXr2SB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012S6jjH2SaixYkicjZmWyru", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01TYUZ9Ggpc8UfhSGYGHHBvz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GFraLGFhX6pYd5Wm1Wz6Nn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The rollback stopped partway through: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to a known-healthy version is safe to repeat, so I'll try it once more.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_015y48szmshRNmuY6i8yeokV", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01N9EHYaxw9dd6XU7oaypn9P", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01BMVSuknRDEGT3hajMFW2sC", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Vg82vL7oDD2Pdd6Un3Dqu3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. Release history: v2.2.9 healthy, v2.3.0 healthy, v2.3.1-rc unhealthy, v2.3.1 unhealthy. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt partially failed: it stopped after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving regions on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A second rollback attempt finished in all regions. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 regression (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy, so check why it was promoted) and look into the orchestrator error during the rollout."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01SHF1tFmTi2zxtAx1ji5Zyg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001. The service is healthy again, with the error rate down from about 18% to 0.2%.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy. v2.3.1 and its release candidate, v2.3.1-rc, were both unhealthy.\n  - The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left the regions on different versions: us-east on v2.3.0, us-west and eu-west still on v2.3.1.\n  - Repeating a rollback to a healthy version is safe, so I ran it again. This time it finished, and all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) are now on v2.3.0.\n- **Incident:** My request to create the incident timed out. Before retrying, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so I didn't retry. That avoided a second page to the on-call engineer.\n  - INC-0001 covers what went wrong, the rollback and the partial failure, and the current state.\n  - It lists two follow-ups: find the cause of the v2.3.1 problem (including why the release went out when its candidate was already unhealthy), and investigate the orchestrator error.", "type": "text"}]}]}